    "Title": "InterDILI: drug-induced injury prediction",
    "Description": "Assesses the risk that a compound causes drug-induced liver injury, the single largest cause of safety-driven withdrawals. InterDILI pairs molecular fingerprints with an attention mechanism so that the substructures driving each prediction can be inspected, and uses permutation feature importance to rank which descriptors matter overall. Lee and Yoo built it for interpretability rather than raw accuracy alone. Ersilia distributes a replicated implementation trained following the published methodology.",
